Market Participants and Scheduling Coordinators:

The California ISO has received the attached request for data from the
Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) in the context of FERC's Bulk
Power Investigation (the nationwide fact-finding probe of electric markets
and recent price spikes).  To the extent the request includes a request for
information that is listed in ISO tariff section 20.3.2., the ISO will seek
confidential treatment for such information pursuant to 18 C.F.R. 388.112.

Any concerns relating to the data request should be communicated by noon on
Friday, October 6 to Jeanne Sole at 916-608-7144 and jsole@caiso.com and
copied to Beth Ann Burns at bburns@caiso.com, Charlie Robinson at
crobinson@caiso.com and Norma Formanek at nformanek@fbm.com.  The FERC
contact on this request is Robert Pease at (202) 208-0131,
robert.pease@ferc.fed.us.


Don Fuller
Director, Client Relations
California ISO



