Mary:

 I would have responded to your message sooner, but it has taken me
these several days to recover from it.  I am surprised and disappointed for
myself and the rest of us here.  You have been a mainstay of the energy
practice and indeed the entire industry for the several years that you have
been out here, and it is difficult to imagine carrying on without you.  Your
legal skills, knowledge of the industry and honest and honorable approach to
dealing with people have, frankly, made you indispensable and irreplaceable.

 That being said, I am happy for you.  I know that you hail from New
England, and you must be glad to be returning.  Western Massachusetts is a
lovely place, and you will be able to pick from any number of attractive
college towns, such as Northampton and Amherst, within an easy commute of
Holyoke.  ISO New England is fortunate to be getting you, and I know you
will thrive there.

 I hope that you will keep in touch, and I look forward to our paths
crossing in the near future.

       Eric


